// THE WINDOWS TARGET, 64-BIT (ADR 0039, 0080, 0093, 0122): the win32 base's
// x86_64 member. NO PORTABILITY CLAIM beyond the language's: Win32's own names
// are this target's.
//
//   glue win32     the base: Win32 over T_LLVM[Σ_OS] (targets/win32), glued
//   x64.oro        the ISA's own operations, at 64 bits (ADR 0103, 0108)
glue win32

// THE TRIPLE (ADR 0093 item 5), what the printer writes: 64-bit Windows,
// MSVC's ABI. 32-bit Windows is targets/windows32, the other member.
triple "x86_64-pc-windows-msvc"

// THE ADDRESS SPACE BOUNDS EVERY TABLE (ADR 0096): x64's user space is 2⁴⁷ bytes,
// and a table of n elements of w ≥ 1 bytes occupies n·w + 8 of them, so n ≤ 2⁴⁷ − 9.
// A fact of the host, as the JVM's `arraylength` is (java.oro).
fact max_len (a ∈ Array(A)) len(a) <= (2^47-9)

build "cmd /c .\\build.bat"
